# No duplicate Vercel production deploys

Pushing to `main` already triggers **one** Production deploy via GitHub → Vercel.

## Do not

- Run `npx vercel --prod`, `vercel --prod --yes`, or `npm run deploy` after `git push` to `main`
- Redeploy the same commit from the Vercel dashboard “just to be sure”
- CLI-deploy with a dirty working tree (`gitDirty`) — that creates “Based on commit … with additional modifications” builds

## Do

- After commit + push to `main`, wait for the Git-triggered deploy to finish
- Only use CLI production deploy if the user explicitly asks **and** the Git deploy failed or never started
- Prefer `git push` alone for shipping; see `docs/VERCEL-BUILD-COSTS.md`

Each extra Production build bills Build CPU (currently Enhanced 8 vCPU — wall time × 8).
